.git/ is a slightly odd place to put a working file, but the
alternatives are worse: the worktree needs a gitignore entry the host
repo has not agreed to, and a temp file outside the repo is gone by the
time anyone wants to see what was scored. Git already keeps
COMMIT_EDITMSG there.

The draft is left in place after the commit. It costs nothing and gives
`git commit --amend -F` something to start from when the message needs a
fix.
